01:07:36.100 --> 01:07:41.620
and this change happens in the third monitoring cycle, okay?

01:07:42.480 --> 01:07:44.400
So, what we have here,

01:07:44.580 --> 01:07:45.820
here, we have the situation

01:07:45.820 --> 01:07:52.620
where the new status is going to be 8, 8, okay?

01:07:53.840 --> 01:07:55.080
It's going to be 8, 8

01:07:55.080 --> 01:07:59.520
because we have 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, okay?

01:08:00.300 --> 01:08:00.780
Great.

01:08:01.580 --> 01:08:03.380
The situation stays the same.

01:08:03.500 --> 01:08:08.900
Here, we have 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8,

01:08:08.900 --> 01:08:11.380
and we get here that we are still 8, 8.

01:08:12.500 --> 01:08:15.180
Once again, we have a fourth monitoring cycle

01:08:15.180 --> 01:08:18.560
where we don't know if the test is present or not.

01:08:18.700 --> 01:08:23.860
So, we will have a status of C8

01:08:23.860 --> 01:08:26.900
because the bit six goes to one

01:08:26.900 --> 01:08:29.260
and everything is 1, 0, 0, 0.

01:08:29.800 --> 01:08:32.620
And then, once we have this test that passes,

01:08:32.740 --> 01:08:33.500
because once again,

01:08:33.640 --> 01:08:38.520
here, we don't have the fault reason anymore,

01:08:39.600 --> 01:08:40.620
this will become...

01:08:43.100 --> 01:08:47.300
And, okay, here, it depends on the fault management,

01:08:48.200 --> 01:08:49.780
lump fault management, okay?

01:08:50.100 --> 01:08:52.340
