01:08:56.340 --> 01:08:58.560
without an error present,

01:08:59.020 --> 01:09:01.100
then also the lump will turn off.

01:09:01.400 --> 01:09:02.800
You will see that there is a

01:09:02.800 --> 01:09:04.100
mill-on-1 management,

01:09:04.760 --> 01:09:07.100
mill-on-2 management,

01:09:07.340 --> 01:09:08.940
mill-on-3 management,

01:09:09.300 --> 01:09:10.700
mill-off management.

01:09:11.040 --> 01:09:15.120
So, we have different kinds of management for lumps.

01:09:15.620 --> 01:09:16.480
Mill-off, of course,

01:09:16.540 --> 01:09:18.120
it means there is no need for a lump.

01:09:18.720 --> 01:09:19.900
Mill-on-1, it means that

01:09:19.900 --> 01:09:22.080
the lump will turn on immediately,

01:09:22.080 --> 01:09:25.140
and turn on immediately.

01:09:25.440 --> 01:09:26.060
Mill-on-2,

01:09:26.700 --> 01:09:29.080
it means that the lump will turn on

01:09:29.080 --> 01:09:30.720
after two cycles with the error.

01:09:30.820 --> 01:09:31.540
And mill-on-3,

01:09:31.660 --> 01:09:33.400
it means that the lump will turn on

01:09:33.400 --> 01:09:35.500
after three cycles when we have the fault.

01:09:35.960 --> 01:09:38.080
But then, for the...

01:09:38.080 --> 01:09:38.920
There should be...

01:09:38.920 --> 01:09:40.120
There is a different management

01:09:40.120 --> 01:09:41.940
to turning off the lump.

01:09:42.520 --> 01:09:43.860
And the turning off of lamps

01:09:43.860 --> 01:09:47.880
usually happens after three monitoring cycles

01:09:47.880 --> 01:09:49.640
without a fault.

